 "reasons": "All eight pictures keep the donor's outline, facing and main parts (pot-still dome with riveted collar, cylindrical tank, chute, belts) in a painted, weathered register with no drawn keyline, matching the smelter sibling's style and scale. Wrecked reads as dead and broken open with dark breaches and nothing lit; Kludged reads as patched and running, with plates, spliced cables, a strapped-on box, a few amber lamps, and clear belts and no open fire breach, which keeps both owner notes on the smelter. At 32 px per cell both tiers read as a dome and a tank in a darker block, clearly apart from the tan ground. The four facings agree on size and palette; the belts overhang the 3x3 footprint only as far as the donor's own belts do within the 4x4 draw size. Real alpha, no ground shadow or scenery.",
 "notes": []
